cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CMSTG: Curvature-Memory Scalar-Tensor Gravity"
abstract: >
  A Lagrangian-based framework for curvature memory and modified gravity.
  CMSTG is a covariant scalar-tensor extension of GR in which spacetime
  curvature couples to a non-local scalar field Psi through a retarded
  Green's function, producing curvature memory. Dark energy emerges from
  the Psi-geometry coupling without a bare cosmological constant. Two
  structural no-go theorems (Paper I) prove that the 2.77-sigma DESI Y1
  BAO residual is irreducible within the CMSTG action class without
  pre-recombination new physics. A completeness probe (SIM144) confirms
  the no-go extends to all curvature-sourced, late-time H(z), and
  mixed-source scalar mechanisms (SIM131-SIM144, exhaustive).
